Alembic migrations for riskview.

They live inside the package so they ship with the wheel and `alembic upgrade
head` works from an installed app, not only from a source checkout. alembic.ini
at the repo root points here and deliberately carries no sqlalchemy.url — env.py
takes it from riskview.config, so migrations and the running app can never
disagree about which database they mean.

    uv run alembic upgrade head                          # apply
    uv run alembic revision --autogenerate -m "..."      # write a new one, then review it
    uv run alembic check                                 # models vs migrations

Revisions are emitted with render_as_batch, because SQLite implements ALTER as a
table rebuild. That rebuild needs every constraint to have a deterministic name,
which is what the naming convention in db/base.py provides.
